%description:

Two things the radio model must not depend on: where the network sits, and
which way it faces.

Neither has an expected value. The scenario is run three times -- as placed,
translated by a kilometre, and rotated a quarter turn about the base station
-- and every recorded scalar of the transformed runs has to equal the
reference run's, bit for bit. A metamorphic check of this shape is unusually
good at catching what a large refactoring actually breaks: an absolute
coordinate that creeps into a formula which should only see a difference, or
an axis convention that stops being a convention.

Fading and shadowing are deliberately left ON. With them off the check would
only exercise the path-loss geometry; with them on it also covers the
per-link state -- the shadowing recurrence keyed on distance travelled, the
Jakes map lookups -- which is the part a refactoring re-homes and the part
that would notice if a map key started depending on absolute position.

The transformations are chosen so that exactness is a fair demand. A
translation by a whole number of metres and a quarter turn both map the
coordinates onto exactly representable ones, so the distances the model
computes are not merely close but identical, and the comparison can be for
equality rather than to a tolerance. A 45 degree rotation would not be a
weaker property, only a weaker test: the differences it produced would be
floating-point noise rather than evidence.

Three UEs at different distances and bearings, so the rotation moves all of
them and the invariance cannot hold by accident of symmetry. One cell and
omnidirectional antennas, because a sectorial antenna has a direction and is
entitled to care which way the network faces.

The configuration pins seed-set, which matters more here than anywhere else
in this directory: OMNeT++ derives it from the run number by default, so the
points of a parameter study would otherwise draw different random numbers and
every stochastic quantity would differ between them -- enough for the model
to appear to violate both invariances by several decibels.

%extraargs: -c GeometryInvariance

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config GeometryInvariance]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.SingleCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 5s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false

# Load-bearing, and the whole test is worthless without it: seed-set defaults
# to the run number, so the points of a parameter study normally get DIFFERENT
# random seeds. An invariance check compares runs against each other, which
# only means anything if they draw the same random numbers -- otherwise every
# stochastic quantity differs and the model looks broken when it is not.
seed-set = 0

############### The transformations ##############
# One at a time: translate, or rotate, or neither.
**.offset = ${dx = 0, 1000}
**.turn = ${rot = 0, 90}
constraint = ($dx == 0) || ($rot == 0)

############### Geometry ##############
# A quarter turn about the base station maps (x,y) to (-y,x), written out
# rather than computed, so the coordinates stay exactly representable.
*.gnb.mobility.initialX = 900m + ${dx}m
*.gnb.mobility.initialY = 900m + ${dx}m
*.gnb.mobility.initialZ = 25m

*.numUe = 3
*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[*].nrServingNodeId = 1
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 900m + ${dx}m + (${rot} == 0 ? 150m : 0m)
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 900m + ${dx}m + (${rot} == 0 ? 0m : 150m)
*.ue[1].mobility.initialX = 900m + ${dx}m + (${rot} == 0 ? 0m : -300m)
*.ue[1].mobility.initialY = 900m + ${dx}m + (${rot} == 0 ? 300m : 0m)
*.ue[2].mobility.initialX = 900m + ${dx}m + (${rot} == 0 ? -450m : 0m)
*.ue[2].mobility.initialY = 900m + ${dx}m + (${rot} == 0 ? 0m : -450m)
*.ue[*].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 3000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 3000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: randomness left on, on purpose ##############
**.scenario = "URBAN_MACROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 25m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = true
**.fading = true
**.fadingType = "JAKES"
**.shadowing = true
**.downlinkInterference = false
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
**.numBands = 6

############### Traffic ##############
*.ue[*].numApps = 1
*.server.numApps = 3
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[*].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[*].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[*].destAddress = "ue[" + string(ancestorIndex(0)) + "]"
*.server.app[*].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[*].localPort = 3088 + ancestorIndex(0)
*.server.app[*].packetSize = 100B
*.server.app[*].samplingTime = 0.01s
*.server.app[*].startTime = 0.1s

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=2 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
